  "_comment": "Hand placement for the painted maps, in grid cells. The generator reads this, classifies every cell from the painting inside the open regions, applies these corrections, and writes shared/src/content/maps/<id>.json. Open regions say where play happens at all; blocked rectangles are the painted structures no classifier can be trusted to find - a tavern, a cauldron, a stream. Everything else - the shrubs, the puddles, the boulder piles - comes from the pixels. Positions were read off the paintings cell by cell; the thresholds were measured, not guessed.",
